    "body": "## Problem\n\nDescribe the problem (concisely).\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n\n```lua\nvim.o.swapfile = false\nvim.o.shadafile = \"NONE\"\nlocal api = vim.api\n\nlocal _n = 0\nlocal _stub_cb_winleave = function()\n\t_n = _n + 1\n\tif _n ~= 3 then return end\n\tlocal bs = api.nvim_list_bufs()\n\tif #bs > 1 then pcall(api.nvim_buf_delete, bs[#bs], { force = true }) end\nend\n\npcall(vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd, \"WinLeave\", { [\"callback\"] = _stub_cb_winleave })\npcall(vim.cmd, \"tabnew\")\npcall(vim.cmd, \"tabnext\")\npcall(vim.api.nvim_buf_delete, 1, { [\"force\"] = true })\n\n```\n\n```\n#0  0x0000559d0cb52f8f in do_buffer_ext (action=4, start=1, dir=1, count=1, flags=1) at src/nvim/buffer.c:1629\n#1  0x0000559d0cb531ec in do_buffer (action=4, start=1, dir=1, count=1, forceit=1) at src/nvim/buffer.c:1693\n#2  0x0000559d0caf61f4 in nvim_buf_delete (buf=1, opts=0x7ffedbda37a0, err=0x7ffedbda3790) at src/nvim/api/buffer.c:1055\n#3  0x0000559d0cca981a in nlua_api_nvim_buf_delete (lstate=0x7f9006182380) at build/src/nvim/auto/lua_api_c_bindings.generated.h:1441\n#4  0x0000559d0cf5c57a in lj_BC_FUNCC ()\n#5  0x0000559d0cf4589a in lua_pcall (L=0x7f9006182380, nargs=<optimized out>, nresults=0, errfunc=<optimized out>) at lj_api.c:1106\n#6  0x0000559d0cccdaed in nlua_pcall (lstate=0x7f9006182380, nargs=0, nresults=0) at src/nvim/lua/executor.c:329\n#7  0x0000559d0ccd2c91 in nlua_exec_file (path=0x559d403a7250 \"/tmp/tmp/a.lua\") at src/nvim/lua/executor.c:2124\n#8  0x0000559d0cde97bb in do_source_ext (fname=0x7ffedbda4de1 \"/tmp/tmp/a.lua\", check_other=false, is_vimrc=0, ret_sid=0x0, eap=0x0, ex_lua=false, str=0x0)\n    at src/nvim/runtime.c:2403\n#9  0x0000559d0cde9cee in do_source (fname=0x7ffedbda4de1 \"/tmp/tmp/a.lua\", check_other=false, is_vimrc=0, ret_sid=0x0) at src/nvim/runtime.c:2495\n#10 0x0000559d0cce36ae in source_startup_scripts (parmp=0x7ffedbda3ca0) at src/nvim/main.c:2233\n#11 0x0000559d0ccde79f in main (argc=10, argv=0x7ffedbda3f28) at src/nvim/main.c:475\n```\n\n## System info\n\n- Nvim version (nvim -v): `v0.13.0-dev-1142 g26357692c8` neovim/neovim@26357692c8\n- Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?: ?\n- Operating system/version: Linux 7.1.5-zen1-1-zen\n- Terminal name/version: kitty\n- $TERM environment variable: `xterm-kitty`\n- Installation: ?\n\n",
